<title>UK: CAI sets warrants on Serbia/Montengro-linked notes.</title>
<headline>CAI sets warrants on Serbia/Montengro-linked notes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Agricole Indosuez said it has issued 2,500 European-style call warrants on an issue of so-called C-3 notes.</p>
<p>C-3 notes, devised by Credit Agricole Indosuez, represent rights to the Serbia and Montengro element of the proceeds of debt linked to the former Yugoslavia.</p>
<p>One warrant controls $100,000 nominal of C-3 notes.</p>
<p>    STRIKE PRICE    28.75 PCT</p>
<p>    ISSUE PRICE     13.375 PCT</p>
<p>    ISSUE DATE	30.JUN.97</p>
<p>    MATURITY DATE   30.JUN.98</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
